{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's sole explicit request (given at the very start of the conversation, before any other turns) was:\n   > \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   \n   No further user messages have been received since then. All constraints come from the spec files themselves: package manager is pnpm only; app served at port 4200 (must not change); do not add dependencies (everything needed is already installed); do not edit `db.json` by hand; desktop-only viewport; all text in English; must use the Angular Material UI library (named in stack.md) for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and datepicker; seat map/legend/selected-seats panel must be hand-drawn by the app itself (not UI library components); exact `data-testid` contract in section 9 must be followed precisely (no renaming/abbreviating/prefixing, and not placed on any other element); and `pnpm nx build cinescope` must succeed by the end.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Angular 22 standalone zoneless app (no NgModules, zoneless change detection, `provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners`).\n   - Angular Signals (`signal`, `computed`, `effect`), `toSignal`/`takeUntilDestroyed` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop`.\n   - Angular Router functional guards (`CanActivateFn`) and functional resolvers (`ResolveFn`), including the newer `RedirectCommand` return type for resolver-based redirects.\n   - Angular Material 22 (MDC-based), legacy button selectors (`mat-button`, `mat-stroked-button`, `mat-flat-button`) confirmed still supported alongside newer `matButton` API; `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent` + `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA` for custom toast content; `MatDatepickerModule` + `provideNativeDateAdapter()` (already present in scaffold).\n   - Reactive Forms (`FormBuilder.nonNullable.group`), custom cross-field and conditional validators, `updateValueAndValidity({onlySelf:true})` pattern for cross-field re-validation.\n   - CSS Grid-based auditorium layout using a fixed 28-track column scheme to guarantee global column alignment across rows (critical for AC-08).\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state persisted via a signal-backed Angular service.\n   - json-server 0.17.4 backend contract (`/movies`, `/screenings`, `/screenings?date=`, `/screenings?movieId=`, `/screenings/:id`, `POST /reservations`).\n   - Strict `data-testid` / `data-*` attribute contract (section 9 of spec) that must be matched exactly.\n   - Sandboxed Bash tool execution environment: discovered that regular (sandboxed) Bash calls appear to get isolated network namespaces that cannot reach `localhost` ports bound by background processes started without `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`, and that even with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`, residual/stale port bindings from earlier sandboxed launches can still cause `EADDRINUSE`-style conflicts (`NX Port 4200 is already in use`).\n   - Playwright-core + pre-existing Chromium binaries at `/opt/ms-playwright` as a way to browser-test without adding a project dependency (installed only into a scratch `/tmp/pw-test` directory, outside the repo).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models.ts`** (created) — `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `ReservationRequest`, `Reservation` interfaces exactly matching spec section 2.1.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/api.service.ts`** (created) — `ApiService` with `getMovies()`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreeningsByDate(date)`, `getScreening(id)`, `createReservation(payload)`, all against `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'` via injected `HttpClient`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/date-utils.ts`** (created) — `toIsoDate`, `startOfToday`, `addDays`, `parseIsoDate` (strict regex + calendar-validity check), `weekdayName`, `monthAbbrev`, `formatShowDate(isoDate, time)` → `\"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\"`, `resolveSelectedDate(dateParam)` (missing/invalid/past → today).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/seats.ts`** (created) — Constants `TOTAL_ROWS=15`, `TOTAL_COLUMNS=24`, `MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING=10`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`. `seatId(row,col)`, `parseSeatId(id)`, `isAccessible(row,col)` (row===1 && col 10-15), `seatPrice(row)` (≤5→25, ≤10→32, else→39), `formatPrice(amount)` → `\"25.00 PLN\"`. `BookingItem` interface and `groupBookingSeats(ids: string[]): BookingItem[]` — the central grouping algorithm reused across seat-map panel, summary, and checkout payload construction; groups by row ascending then column ascending, pairs row-15 columns two-at-a-time into couches.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/auditorium-layout.ts`** (created) — `AuditoriumCell` union type (`seat`/`accessible`/`couch`), `AuditoriumRow` interface, `AISLE_GRID_COLUMNS = [6,23]`, `LABEL_LEFT_GRID_COLUMN = 1`, `LABEL_RIGHT_GRID_COLUMN = 28`, `gridColumnForSeat(column)` mapping formula (col≤4→col+1; col≤20→col+2; else col+3), `buildRow(row)` and exported `AUDITORIUM_ROWS: AuditoriumRow[]` (precomputed once for rows 1-15, with row 1-10 omitting the cols1-4 entrance block, row 15 generating couch cells, row 1 cols 10-15 flagged `accessible`).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.service.ts`** (created) — `CheckoutFormValues` and `BookingState` interfaces; `STORAGE_KEY = 'cinescope.booking'`; `BookingService` (providedIn root) with signal `state` loaded from `sessionStorage` on construction, `persist()` private helper, and public methods `matchesUnpaid`, `hasSeats`, `isPaid`, `selectedSeats`, `seatCount`, `ensureBooking(screeningId)`, `clear`, `addSeats(ids)`, `removeSeats(ids)`, `updateForm(partial)`, `markPaid(email)`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.component.ts`** (created) — Minimal standalone `ToastComponent` rendering `<span data-testid=\"toast\">{{ message }}</span>`, reading `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.service.ts`** (created) — `ToastService` wrapping `MatSnackBar`; `show(message)` calls `snackBar.dismiss()` then `openFromComponent(ToastComponent, { data: {message}, duration: 4000, panelClass: 'app-toast-panel' })`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/screening-resolver.ts`** (created) — `ScreeningData` interface `{screening, movie}`; `screeningResolver: ResolveFn<ScreeningData | RedirectCommand>` fetching screening then movie, `catchError` → `of(new RedirectCommand(router.parseUrl('/')))`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/guards.ts`** (created) — `bookingInProgressGuard` and `paidBookingGuard` functional `CanActivateFn`s.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/core/checkout-validators.ts`** (created) — `emailFormatValidator()`, `phoneFormatValidator()`, `matchesControlValidator(otherControlName)`, using `EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/` and `PHONE_PATTERN = /^\\d{9}$/`, with an `isEmpty()` helper so empty values don't trigger format errors (required handled separately).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`** (edited twice) — Added `provideHttpClient()`. Initially also added `provideAnimationsAsync()` from `'@angular/platform-browser/animations/async'`, which **broke the build** (`Could not resolve \"@angular/animations/browser\"` — package not installed, and must not be added). Removed that import and provider entirely. Final state:\n     ```ts\n     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\n     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';\n     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';\n     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';\n     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';\n\n     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n       providers: [\n         provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),\n         provideRouter(appRoutes),\n         provideNativeDateAdapter(),\n         provideHttpClient(),\n       ],\n     };\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts`** (rewritten) — Final route table as described in section 6 of this analysis (5 routes + wildcard redirect, with `screeningResolver` attached to seats/summary/checkout routes and guards on summary/checkout/confirmation).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/day-picker.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `DayPickerComponent`, input `selectedDate` (required signal input), output `dateSelected`. Computed `quickDays` (today + 4 days). Template renders 5 `mat-stroked-button`s with `data-testid=\"day-button\"`, `[attr.data-date]`, `[attr.data-selected]`, plus a `mat-form-field`/`mat-datepicker` with `data-testid=\"date-picker\"`. Fixed bug: originally tried to dynamically toggle between `mat-flat-button`/`mat-stroked-button` directive selectors via `[attr.mat-flat-button]`/`[attr.mat-stroked-button]` bindings — this is invalid because Angular directive matching happens at compile time based on static attributes, not bound values; fixed by always using `mat-stroked-button` and toggling a CSS class (`day-button--selected`) + `[color]` instead.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/movie-list.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `MovieListComponent` using `toSignal(route.queryParamMap, {requireSync:true})`, `resolveSelectedDate`, `effect()`-driven loading via `forkJoin([getMovies(), getScreeningsByDate(date)])`, `status` signal, grouping/sorting logic, `onDateSelected`, `retry`, `openSeatMap`. Template covers all section 9.1 testids.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-map/seat-map.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `SeatMapComponent` as detailed in section 5 of analysis above; full code includes `idsForCell`, `stateFor`, `gridColumnFor`, `labelFor`, `onCellClick`, `cancel`, `continue`, `legend` array, `selectedRowLines` computed. SCSS defines the 28-track grid (`$seat: 2rem; $aisle: 4rem; $label: 1.5rem;`) and an `@each` loop over a `$colors` SCSS map applying background colors to `.seat[data-state=...]`, `.couch[data-state=...]`, `.swatch[data-state=...]`, with a `&:focus-visible { outline: ... }` rule and no `:hover` background rule (ensuring hover/focus don't change seat colors per spec).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/summary/summary.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `SummaryComponent` using `groupBookingSeats`, `seatDescription(item)`, `remove(item)` (navigates to seat map if booking becomes empty), `back()`, `confirm()`. Template covers all section 9.3 testids.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/checkout.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `CheckoutComponent` as detailed in section 5 above; full code includes the reactive form definition, `errorMessage(name)` generic error-key-to-message mapping, `labelFor(name)`, `onTermsChange()`, `back()`, `pay()`. Template covers all section 9.4 testids, with labels ending in `*` for the five required fields and plain `Phone number` for the optional one.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/features/confirmation/confirmation.component.ts`** (created) + **`.html`** + **`.scss`** — `ConfirmationComponent` with `email` property from `booking.booking()?.email`, `continue()` clearing booking and navigating to `/`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`NG5002: @for loop must have a \"track\" expression`** in `seat-map.component.html` for `@for (column of aisleColumns) { ... }` — fixed by changing to `@for (column of aisleColumns; track column) { ... }`.\n   - **`Could not resolve \"@angular/animations/browser\"`** build failure caused by `provideAnimationsAsync()` in `app.config.ts` — root cause: `@angular/animations` is not in the installed dependency tree (confirmed via `node -e \"console.log(require('./node_modules/@angular/material/package.json').peerDependencies)\"` and `ls node_modules/@angular`), and the spec forbids adding dependencies. Fixed by removing `provideAnimationsAsync()` and its import entirely; the app now runs without Angular's animation module.\n   - After both fixes, `pnpm nx build cinescope` (actually required `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope` the first time, because plain `pnpm nx build cinescope` hit `[ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]` when pnpm wanted to recreate `node_modules` without a TTY) succeeded with exit code 0, producing only a non-fatal bundle-size warning (696.57 kB initial bundle vs. 500kB warning budget; well under the 1MB hard error budget), confirmed via a second `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope` run showing `EXIT=0` with a cache hit.\n   - **Ongoing, unresolved**: During manual browser-verification (not a build error, but a local dev-environment/tooling issue), background-started `pnpm api` and `pnpm nx serve cinescope` processes could not be reached via `fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')` / `fetch('http://localhost:4200')` from separate Bash tool invocations, even after passing `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Diagnosed partially via `/proc/net/tcp` and `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` (no `ps